Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:06.50,Default,,0,0,800,,{\b1\4c&H0000FF&\fs40}LAUGHING MAN FANSUBS{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.89,0:00:09.79,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I'm a soldier - that means I'm
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.99,0:00:13.19,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Both a defendant and the judge
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.59,0:00:18.59,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I am standing on both ends of the flame
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.27,0:00:23.37,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Rounding curves
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.57,0:00:26.27,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Overtaking life and death,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.77,0:00:31.87,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I run and fight with false shadows
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.17,0:00:38.77,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,No matter how many threads of\Ndeception are woven together,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.07,0:00:46.57,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,The truth shall illuminate the face of light
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.07,0:00:49.87,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save your tears for the day
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.47,0:00:53.47,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,when our pain is far behind
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.57,0:00:56.67,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,on your feet, come with me
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.77,0:01:00.07,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,We are soldiers stand or die
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.27,0:01:03.47,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save your fears, take your place
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.37,0:01:06.37,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save them for the judgement day
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.67,0:01:09.57,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,fast and free, follow me
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.87,0:01:14.63,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Time to make the sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.67,0:01:20.67,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,We rise or fall
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.47,0:01:49.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,F-4 decoys activated!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.07,0:01:51.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Barrier dismantling viruses injected!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.57,0:01:53.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.57,0:01:57.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Once you've put our offensive firewalls\Non standby at all the external firewalls,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.37,0:01:59.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,activate protection and freeze it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.27,0:02:00.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Roger!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.77,0:02:02.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Found it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.67,0:02:09.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So, a stealth gate that must traverse Europe's\Nsatellite network via the northern hemisphere...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.07,0:02:10.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.97,0:02:12.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But it's nothing serious.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.47,0:02:14.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's actually an Asian matrix.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.87,0:02:16.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So, a local Asian net.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.77,0:02:18.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Not sophisticated at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.27,0:02:19.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Nope.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.47,0:02:22.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Shall we begin the structural analysis right away?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.77,0:02:24.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Contact the Major first.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.76,0:02:32.12,Sign - Copy,,600,0,550,,{\b1}To Those \N Without Even \Na Name{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.90,0:02:35.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Gouda's showing off, isn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.80,0:02:38.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's a message that we won't\Nfind proof that leads to him
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.50,0:02:42.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,even if we find Kawashima's external memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.10,0:02:43.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How clever.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.80,0:02:44.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, from the looks of it,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.80,0:02:48.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,there is no trace that a third party\Nhas tampered with this external memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.20,0:02:52.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If we are to presume that the Individual\NEleven phenomenon is the result of a virus,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.20,0:02:55.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,there is a significant\Nchance that evidence remains.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.20,0:02:58.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right, I'll dive.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.30,0:03:01.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Ishikawa and Bomer, cover me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.70,0:03:03.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Tachikoma, have the viral array on standby.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.70,0:03:05.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How about the D set?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.90,0:03:06.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.20,0:03:10.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major, I'm sorry to interrupt,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.60,0:03:11.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but I need you ASAP.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.10,0:03:13.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This is top priority.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.80,0:03:17.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Since it has higher priority than\Nthis, it can't be good.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.50,0:03:18.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.50,0:03:20.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Call Batou, Saitou and Pazu as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.20,0:03:23.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You heard him.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.30,0:03:27.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Bomer, make the dive in my place.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.10,0:03:29.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Ishikawa, please take care of the rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.87,0:03:38.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right, let's get this over with.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.53,0:03:47.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.53,0:03:55.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.43,0:03:59.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Togusa-kun, why don't you put\Nyour personified data on default?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.23,0:04:00.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.13,0:04:01.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, it may be different if\Nwe're talking about chats.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.53,0:04:02.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but don't you think it'd be too dangerous
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.03,0:04:05.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to lug something heavy like that around\Nwhen you're diving into a firewall array?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.53,0:04:07.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Besides, do you really want to see me and\Nold man Ishikawa looking out of place,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.83,0:04:11.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,wearing costumes like\NAmerican comic book heroes?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.43,0:04:13.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You have a point there...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.13,0:04:14.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Cut the chit-chat.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.93,0:04:16.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Bomer's about to go through the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.67,0:04:23.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Resuming viral injection!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.67,0:04:27.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Collision with enemy's firewall array and\Ncommencement of neutralisation confirmed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.20,0:04:32.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How is it going?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.20,0:04:34.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's starting to become visible.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.30,0:04:36.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There's a suspicious file on level six.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.00,0:04:38.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What's the name of the file?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.70,0:04:40.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,"Individual Eleven."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.50,0:04:41.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What now?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.80,0:04:46.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then, if we are to confirm whether that's the\Nvirus that triggers the Individual Eleven,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.70,0:04:50.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It'd be quickest to drop that\Nfile into someone's cyberbrain.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.40,0:04:51.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.60,0:04:51.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh well.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.50,0:04:53.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I guess I'll try putting it in my head.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.80,0:04:56.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, isn't it dangerous?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.50,0:04:59.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Wouldn't it be better to build a vaccine first?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.70,0:05:02.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You can't make vaccines\Nuntil after symptoms develop.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.50,0:05:04.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's how it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.60,0:05:07.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right, the backup is complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.10,0:05:11.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Just in case, partition off your\Ncyberbrain's analysis sectors.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.80,0:05:12.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yep.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.00,0:05:24.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This is footage that was recorded twenty-two minutes\Nago by the IR system on Nagasaki's offshore reef.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.97,0:05:30.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Man, where has he been hiding all this time?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.87,0:05:33.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If he hadn't switched to a new cybernetic body,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.17,0:05:36.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,it could be that he was inactive\Nuntil his body parts regenerated.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.47,0:05:41.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This could be our chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.77,0:05:46.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I have requested that the authorities in Kyushu\Nbolster their surveillance of the entire region.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.67,0:05:49.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Go to Nagasaki ASAP and secure him!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.57,0:05:56.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, Bomer...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.87,0:05:57.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.77,0:06:02.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, isn't this bad?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.47,0:06:04.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We'll terminate the program by force.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.37,0:06:12.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, Bomer!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.50,0:06:23.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.60,0:06:24.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.00,0:06:26.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So, how was it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.60,0:06:28.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Nothing special.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.10,0:06:30.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The contents were a poorly constructed essay.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.10,0:06:32.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Essay?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.71,0:06:45.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If that man is the same one who\Nattacked the Prime Minister,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.01,0:06:47.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,then as the Chief said,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.41,0:06:50.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,it's quite possible that the factor\Nthat caused the Individual
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.41,0:06:53.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Eleven's appearance is still\Nfully retained in his cyberbrain.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.48,0:06:57.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We could use long distance sniping,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.68,0:07:02.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but PKF-spec bodies are immortal prosthetics whose\Norgans each operate independently.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.18,0:07:04.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They can't be stopped unless\Nyou shoot them in the head.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.38,0:07:07.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If that's the case, we'll get\Nclose and overwhelm him by force.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.78,0:07:11.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Depending on the situation, I can\Nuse this and just take the head back.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.25,0:07:14.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Quite a sadist, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.16,0:07:25.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I wonder if symptoms won't develop\Njust by downloading this thing...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.66,0:07:27.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,After all, there's no point in\Nrandomly scattering this around
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.96,0:07:31.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and turning everyone into an Individual Eleven.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.96,0:07:34.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It could be that there are other factors involved.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.10,0:07:36.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How's it going?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.64,0:07:37.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Not very good.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.54,0:07:43.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Gouda's plans, which the Major found\Nafter diving in, were very credible.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.04,0:07:46.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,His plans ignited the fury of the refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.74,0:07:49.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He's responsible all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.84,0:07:54.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In addition, it seems he can't wait to\Nhave someone else discovers his methods.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.94,0:07:59.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But, unless he displays\Nsymptoms, we can prove nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.34,0:08:04.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If we could at least get our hands on the\Noriginal "Individual Eleven" essay...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.44,0:08:07.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But they couldn't find it the last\Ntime they searched either, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.44,0:08:11.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then how about trying to find it in paper?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.44,0:08:15.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The original document may\Nstill be around somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.44,0:08:16.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,True.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.54,0:08:18.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I have a place in mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.44,0:08:19.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Try there.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.04,0:08:21.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.24,0:08:23.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right, I'll leave that to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.94,0:08:29.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Bomer and I will do another complete\Nanalysis on Kawashima's external memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.24,0:08:32.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's the only lead we have right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.64,0:08:34.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right, I'm counting on you two.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.64,0:08:35.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.78,0:08:41.27,Dialogue,,0,0,225,,{\b1\i1}Okinawa Prefecture Monument{\b0\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.04,0:08:48.74,Dialogue,,200,0,750,,{\b1\i1}Foreign War \N Casualties Monument{\b0\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.87,0:08:52.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Stop that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.77,0:08:59.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Save these feelings for the\Nactions we'll be taking.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.07,0:09:02.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I concur.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.37,0:09:05.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems the others are also gathering.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.97,0:09:07.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We don't have time.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.63,0:09:17.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We lost track of him?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.03,0:09:18.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.33,0:09:25.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We were able to confirm from the highway's\NIR system that he headed towards Kagoshima,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.23,0:09:29.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but after he pulled over at a rest stop, he\Nmay have switched his car to remote control,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.13,0:09:32.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,then hid himself in a freight\Ntruck heading elsewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.13,0:09:37.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The staff from the monitoring centre appear\Nto have continued their pursuit of the car.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.63,0:09:40.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Where did his car go after that?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.63,0:09:43.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The car left the interchange\Nand went towards Fukuoka.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.43,0:09:46.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What about hacking the car's\NAI and putting a trace on him?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.93,0:09:50.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The moment we tried to connect,\Nthe network got cut off.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.43,0:09:54.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So he knows something about cyberspace warfare.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.23,0:09:59.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.83,0:10:06.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Pursue all the freight trucks that\Nappear in this footage and find him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.43,0:10:07.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.13,0:10:09.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What now?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.13,0:10:10.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We will head to Kagoshima.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.73,0:10:13.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,And what if this a trap he\Nrigged to make you think that?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.03,0:10:16.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If we consider the possibilities,\NKagoshima is highest on the list.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.27,0:10:31.80,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,{\b1\i1}Kagoshima Prefecture War \N Casualties Monument Tower{\b0\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.72,0:10:39.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Is this everyone?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.42,0:10:46.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Anyone who shares the particularist\Nwill would not arrive any later.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.35,0:11:12.35,Dialogue,,0,400,650,,{\b1\i1}Niihama University \N Sociology Department{\b0\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.69,0:11:17.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I came with Chief Aramaki's recommendation.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.89,0:11:19.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,My name is Togusa.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.49,0:11:20.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes, I've heard of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.29,0:11:24.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You wanted to see the original\N"Individual Eleven." correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.79,0:11:28.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes. I couldn't find it on the net,\Nno matter how hard I looked, so...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.99,0:11:30.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Not surprisingly.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.79,0:11:35.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The "Individual Eleven" is a very\Nvaluable book by Patrick Sylvestre
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.19,0:11:37.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,written after he invested himself\Nin the Romanian Revolution
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.79,0:11:39.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,right before his death.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.89,0:11:44.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Only twenty copies were published.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.19,0:11:50.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,A significant number of translated editions\Nshould have been reprinted by now, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.95,0:11:55.25,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The author himself seems to\Nhave locked the text away
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.35,0:12:00.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,because he couldn't conclusively define the 515 Incident\Nin Japan as having been a revolution until the very end.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.65,0:12:03.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I have heard that his thought processes, which\Ninclude using Noh as a metaphor for revolution,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.55,0:12:07.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,still retain their brilliance today.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.05,0:12:12.25,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It doesn't seem like you're\Nhere with a snobby attitude.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.55,0:12:13.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.05,0:12:18.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Since you do also have Aramaki-san's referral I'll\Nmake a special exception and show it to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.95,0:12:21.25,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.50,0:12:26.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How is it going?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.80,0:12:29.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, I think I got him to trust me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.00,0:12:34.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That aside, I'm surprised that this stuffy\Nprofessor is an acquaintance of yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.10,0:12:37.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Times may change,\Nbut it'll always be about networking.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.10,0:12:39.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,True.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.40,0:12:40.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How strange...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.80,0:12:46.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'd never taken it out of this\Nroom since I obtained it, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.70,0:12:50.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Um, it doesn't have to be the original.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.50,0:12:53.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It can be a copy or a reprint...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.50,0:12:57.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, for some reason,\NI see no sign of it at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.31,0:13:20.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,By the way, how did you assert yourself?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.21,0:13:27.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I just stabbed an enemy of the state, a Diet member who\Nwas advocating a conciliatory policy towards refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.51,0:13:28.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,And you?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.91,0:13:32.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We infiltrated the JNN TV accounting network
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.01,0:13:36.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and made it seem as though they were misappropriating funds\Nthat were set aside for charities assisting refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.71,0:13:38.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.71,0:13:44.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We used a more direct approach to\Nprompt the liberation of refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.31,0:13:50.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The bombing of the refugee support organisation,\NKinan Association, was how we asserted ourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.51,0:13:53.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The media gave a lot of press to\Nthe Kinan Association bombing,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.91,0:13:56.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but all it did was to sever ties between refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.31,0:14:01.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We got rid of a true enemy of the state, a traitor.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.31,0:14:05.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We targeted the NPO that was providing\Nrefugees with free cybernetic bodies.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.51,0:14:09.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Though it seems you failed to\Ncarry out a successful bombing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.41,0:14:12.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Certainly, striking down a traitor is amusing too,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.11,0:14:15.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but what matters is severing the arteries of the\Nrefugees who ought to be liberated.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.11,0:14:18.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What have you done, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.71,0:14:21.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I took the netbank president's head.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.91,0:14:26.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You're the one who got President Jima Ichihiro, who\Nmade his fortune through the netbank he created,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.11,0:14:29.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,even though he was born a refugee?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.21,0:14:35.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,While I haven't done as much as you in the way\Nof severing these so-called support lines,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.21,0:14:39.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,in terms of having an impact on the public, what\NI've done does not take a back seat to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.11,0:14:43.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I am the one who killed the\Npopular cyber-rapper, "Densetsu".
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.21,0:14:45.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,And one more thing:
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.31,0:14:49.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I also spread the rumour that the\Nrefugees would try to take the fuel rod
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.81,0:14:53.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,that was dug up from the\Ngovernment's secret nuclear plant.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.21,0:14:54.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Impressive.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.21,0:14:59.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Those events did in fact have a major impact\Non both the citizens and the refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.11,0:15:03.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Densetsu was a pillar of psychological\Nsupport for the refugee youths.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.51,0:15:07.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It was natural that hatred took root in\Ntheir hearts when he was lost to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.91,0:15:10.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,On top of that, you spread a rumour\Nthat would incite a mass uprising.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.91,0:15:14.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Our actions pale in comparison to yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.21,0:15:16.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Unfortunately, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.91,0:15:20.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, in terms of how we severed the\Nrefugees' support, by killing a physician
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.51,0:15:24.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,who was an enemy of the state,\Nthe significance is the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.95,0:15:28.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How have you asserted yourself?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.45,0:15:34.25,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I tried to assassinate Kayabuki.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.65,0:15:37.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hah.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.75,0:15:40.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You chose a very audacious act.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.15,0:15:43.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, I've never heard of this incident.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.55,0:15:48.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It must have been ignored, as were the\NIndividual Eleven's claims of responsibility.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.15,0:15:50.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That is of trivial importance.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.55,0:15:57.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That aside, this liberation of the refugees you all\Nspeak of only seems to lead them to despair...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.75,0:15:59.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,why is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.15,0:16:04.25,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It is to cut off support from enemies\Nof the state and their compatriots,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.35,0:16:06.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and prompt the liberation known as independence.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.85,0:16:13.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That is the best way to have citizens realise on their own\Nthe existence of the foreign entity called the refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.25,0:16:15.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Is this not true?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.60,0:16:31.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, Ishikawa.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.00,0:16:34.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Have you read all of Sylvestre's essays?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.80,0:16:38.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah, all of them except\Nthe "Individual Eleven."
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.60,0:16:39.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Why do you ask?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.50,0:16:40.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What about you, Chief?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.20,0:16:43.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I actually haven't read any.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.40,0:16:47.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I've also read all of them aside\Nfrom the "Individual Eleven."
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.70,0:16:52.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, it'd be more unusual that someone\Nwould've read all of them in this day and age.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.30,0:16:53.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.30,0:16:57.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But this Kawashima has read them too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.50,0:17:00.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Not only that, but he must have\Nuploaded them to his external memory
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.30,0:17:02.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and memorised every word.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.20,0:17:04.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.30,0:17:07.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.50,0:17:09.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.20,0:17:13.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So that's the factor that activates the virus.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.80,0:17:15.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Probably.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.10,0:17:20.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Tachikoma, from that external\Nmemory, collect files that pertain
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.67,0:17:23.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to Sylvestre's collection of\Npreliminary theories on revolution.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.32,0:17:24.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Roger!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.82,0:17:43.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major, I found him!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.52,0:17:47.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,it's an image of Kagoshima Prefecture's War\NCasualties Monument Tower that was taken at 14:30.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.52,0:17:51.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right, change direction towards\Nthe War Casualties Monument Tower!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.52,0:17:54.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood, heading towards the\NWar Casualties Monument Tower.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.12,0:18:07.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Chief, no luck here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.42,0:18:10.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The "Individual Eleven" isn't here, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.97,0:18:12.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If it isn't there,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.97,0:18:15.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,there are no further means of finding it, it seems.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.67,0:18:17.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Togusa, come back for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.07,0:18:20.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If we can't find it, we can't find it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.57,0:18:21.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.17,0:18:25.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But I have one more place in mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.27,0:18:26.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'll come back after checking it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.67,0:18:27.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.87,0:18:29.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We've extracted the files!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.27,0:18:30.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right, let's have a go at it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.97,0:18:31.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Roger.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.96,0:18:39.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's almost time.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.46,0:18:40.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.26,0:18:42.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,By the way, who will deliver the final speech?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.16,0:18:47.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The one who was able to propagate our intent the\Nmost would be the one most suitable for the task.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.96,0:18:49.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That would be...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.16,0:18:50.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,you, I presume?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.26,0:18:53.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Among our comrades who did not show up,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.86,0:18:56.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I am sure that there are many\Nwho contributed to our cause,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.06,0:19:01.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but if all of you feel I should, then I\Nwill willingly accept that monumental task.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.06,0:19:04.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You don't have any objections, do you?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.26,0:19:05.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,None.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.46,0:19:09.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, I have one request.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.66,0:19:11.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Our scripture, the "Individual Eleven."
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.96,0:19:14.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If you don't object, could I see yours?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.26,0:19:16.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Is yours the first edition?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.24,0:19:19.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,A moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.77,0:19:26.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If you wanted to know the edition, mine should\Nbe the first edition, if I recall correctly.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.37,0:19:28.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Are you sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.67,0:19:29.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Y-Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.68,0:19:35.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Today, as I proceeded to make my way here,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.98,0:19:39.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I decided to bring a copy of the\N"Individual Eleven" with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.58,0:19:42.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But no matter how hard I\Nlooked, I couldn't find it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.78,0:19:43.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Why is that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.28,0:19:51.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Please, will someone please let\Nme see the "Individual Elev...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.08,0:19:51.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,{\i1}Hey.{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.18,0:19:54.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We're almost there.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.89,0:20:04.78,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,{\b1\i1}Window Sign: Dobashi Fumiya Office{\b1}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.11,0:20:14.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Y-You're that guy from before.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.51,0:20:17.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You're in quite a hurry, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.31,0:20:19.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I actually had another\Nquestion to ask of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.31,0:20:20.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You came at just the right time.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.81,0:20:22.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In any case, come with me!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.21,0:20:23.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,H-H-Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.11,0:20:27.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Stop it! Put that down!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.61,0:20:28.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,{\i1}Please stop!{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.81,0:20:31.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.86,0:20:37.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.76,0:20:39.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Nothing out of the ordinary.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.86,0:20:44.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Maybe we do need the original of the\Nlast essay, the "Individual Eleven."
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.97,0:20:48.38,Sign,,0,0,600,,{\frz10}{\fs60}{\b1}"Individual Eleven"{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.56,0:20:50.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What the?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.73,0:20:55.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Ishikawa!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.63,0:20:59.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Bomer!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.82,0:21:12.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Tachikoma, turn off Bomer's cyberbrain\Nactivity and have him sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.82,0:21:17.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Also, make that file unreadable and\Nseal it off with a firewall array.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.32,0:21:18.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Roger!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.62,0:21:21.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Looks like we got lucky.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.42,0:21:24.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Chief, we have an emergency transmission\Nfrom the Ministry of the Interior.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.22,0:21:27.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Put it through to the Dive Room!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.62,0:21:28.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Roger.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.01,0:21:38.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This is...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.71,0:21:43.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What the hell were they\Ndoing in a place like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.21,0:21:46.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major, go to the Kyushu Communications Tower ASAP!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.01,0:21:48.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He showed up there!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.01,0:21:50.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What is this about?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.31,0:21:53.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I don't know, but Channel W3 has him on camera.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.11,0:21:58.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So they found him?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.11,0:21:59.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,800,,{\i1}Hey, what'd they say?{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.41,0:22:00.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,800,,{\i1}What'd they say?!{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.51,0:22:01.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,800,,{\i1}Bring the camera around!{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.51,0:22:02.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What the hell?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.01,0:22:04.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,800,,{\i1}Oh my god, swords!{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.61,0:22:06.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,800,,{\i1}They're swinging their swords... OH MY GOD!{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.21,0:22:07.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,800,,{\i1}Their heads...{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.31,0:22:09.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,800,,{\i1}They cut off... each other's heads...\Nwith their swords!{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.01,0:22:11.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,800,,{\i1}One after the other... Th... they're fighting!{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.11,0:22:14.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,800,,{\i1}It's an unbelievable sight!{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.71,0:22:18.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,800,,{\i1}The men who appeared on the building's rooftop\Nseem to have killed each other with swords!{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.01,0:22:22.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Please calm down, I just came here to talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.81,0:22:22.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,{\i1}Don't come any closer.{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.81,0:22:26.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You know the essay titled the\N"Individual Eleven", right?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.61,0:22:31.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That "Individual Eleven" essay...\Nnever existed in the first place!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.11,0:22:36.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All that exists... is a manufactured\Ntheory called the "Individual Eleven"!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.21,0:22:40.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I am the Individual Eleven!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.21,0:22:42.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The time has finally come!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.33,0:22:49.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,An ambulance, hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.56,0:23:10.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Finding out a galaxy
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.46,0:23:14.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,of planets and stars within me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.06,0:23:17.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Listening to each of them
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.26,0:23:21.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,singing the same silent melody.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.16,0:23:25.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I've never seen such beauty
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.66,0:23:28.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,in possibility...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.96,0:23:33.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No smack of doubt or fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.56,0:23:35.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(Wake up)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.16,0:23:37.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I hear a voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.99,0:23:39.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(And show the light)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.75,0:23:40.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,hear a voice calling out to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.27,0:23:41.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(Wake up)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.93,0:23:43.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see inside
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.53,0:23:46.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(the time is right)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.56,0:23:47.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,see the light now ever holding me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.96,0:23:49.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All the truth,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.51,0:23:51.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All I need,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.50,0:23:50.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(All the truth)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.98,0:23:53.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to make all this reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:53.60,0:23:54.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(it's inside)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.86,0:23:57.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The beauty within the shell.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.87,0:23:58.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(deep within the shell)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.29,0:24:00.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(within the shell)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.27,0:24:01.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(Wake up)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.85,0:24:03.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I hear a voice
Dialogue: 0,0:24:02.77,0:24:04.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(And show the light)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.55,0:24:08.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,hear a voice calling out to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.86,0:24:08.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(Wake up)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.83,0:24:12.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(the time is now)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.05,0:24:11.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see inside,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:11.25,0:24:14.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,see the light now ever holding me.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.37,0:24:15.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All the truth,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.67,0:24:16.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(All the truth)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:16.10,0:24:17.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,all I need,
